# Scratch space for local Checkly testing. Everything here is gitignored
# except this file and `*.example` siblings.

# Quick-start
# -----------
# 1. Copy .env.example -> .env and fill in your Checkly creds.
# 2. (Recommended) Copy ../examples/consumer-checks.json -> ./my-sandbox.json
#    and change `project.logicalId` to something like
#    `sandbox-<yourname>-checks` so you don't collide with anyone else's
#    Checkly project. Swap the acme.com URLs for URLs you own.
# 3. From the repo root:
#      npm run try                                          # validate, no network
#      npm run try:preview                                  # diff, no apply
#      npm run try:test    -- --config local-testing/my-sandbox.json
#      npm run try:deploy  -- --config local-testing/my-sandbox.json
#
# DEPLOY SAFETY: `try:deploy` actually persists monitors in your Checkly
# account. Use a sandbox account or a unique `project.logicalId` so you
# don't stomp on production. The auto-emitted `source:checkly-templates`
# tag still makes managed checks identifiable in the Checkly UI.
